WEBVTT

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:16.070
So much green! Such clear water!

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:17.740
Mountains covered in trees!

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.240
So much life!

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:23.830
I wonder if the forest of boars{>mononoke} is around here, Hayate!

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:26.420
I'm not so sure about that.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:30.050
The countryside is really nice! I'm so excited!

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:31.840
I can see that.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.220
<i>August 27th.</i>

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:39.930
<i>At the end of our eventful summer break,{i didn't bother all the nandakanda}</i>

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:44.020
<i>we ended up going on a trip to the countryside where Nishizawa was from.</i>

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:48.940
<i>As for the events of our summer break, please read the manga,</i>

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:53.440
<i>but the reason why we're on this trip will be explained later.</i>

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:56.660
<i>She didn't want to come at first, but now...</i>

00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:59.780
Hayate, who are you explaining so enthusiastically to?

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:01.950
We can hear your monologue, you know.

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:05.830
I only want you to understand that milady's tension is really high.

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:08.250
Hey, Hayate!

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:10.090
Do you think Totoro lives here?

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:12.920
T-Totoro?

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:20.140
Yeah! I prepared for the trip by watching lots of anime about summer{fags} and the countryside!

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:25.810
There's <i>gotta</i> be a Totoro or two living here!

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:29.560
I want to catch one, no matter how small, and go home together!

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:32.320
I don't know about that.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:34.320
The countryside is going to be so much fun!

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:36.070
So much fun!

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:42.540
Nagi's being so cute.

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:43.950
I know, right?

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:48.460
Totoros are protected creatures. It's illegal to catch them.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:52.670
This is bad, Arisa! Her idiocy is infiltrating the countryside!

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:56.220
We were too late!

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:02.060
Listen up. It's okay for  Nagi to believe in Totoro because she's only 13,

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:04.930
but it's unacceptable for a 17-year-old like you!

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:07.480
B-But...

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:09.480
What are you talking about?

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:12.820
Nothing!

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:15.150
We hope you'll find Totoro, Nagi!

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:18.070
Yeah! I'll definitely find one!

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:24.290
Maria, do you think milady will be all right?

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:28.210
Her expectations of the countryside seem a bit too high...

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:30.120
The countryside will be so much fun!

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.340
Of course.

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:38.680
I already told you that humans who can't control their emotions are trash.

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:42.930
Kayura, you still have that helmet on?

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:47.100
I want to take it off, but it'd be a spoiler.{seriously}{w}

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:54.570
With such high expectations, she's bound to end up being very disappointed.

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:57.690
I hope it won't end as Ruka said.

00:02:58.070 --> 00:02:59.740
Well...

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:03.120
I see!

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:06.410
I have shows scheduled so I can't go, but you should go and have fun!

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:09.330
I'm sure you'll enjoy the countryside, it's full of bugs!

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:12.880
Full of bugs?

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:18.170
During summer, the countryside looks all peaceful and calm, but it's actually the realm of bugs!

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:23.470
Millions of giant centipedes crawling around.

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:26.810
Gargantuan spiders falling on you from the ceiling!

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:31.440
So have as much fun there as you can, in my stead too!

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:36.730
Are you even disappointed that you couldn't come along?

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:40.450
That's not true!{Not at all!}

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:43.160
I'm not interested in the summer countryside at all!

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:48.080
I can totally imagine you losing it about how loud the cicadas are!

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:53.960
How could I lose it about cicadas?!

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:56.540
<i>That's true.</i>

00:03:56.540 --> 00:04:02.260
<i>If she's disappointed again, she'll revert back to being a shut-in.</i>

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:09.060
<i>As her butler, it's my duty to help her become a nature-loving countryside girl!</i>

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:19.570
We're here! Finally!

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:23.320
Amazing!

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:26.910
This is the real Japanese countryside!

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:30.410
So tranquil!

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:32.370
Yes!

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:39.710
See, Milady? This is the countryside you have been waiting for!

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:43.130
Hayate, it's so hot...

00:04:43.130 --> 00:04:44.760
I think I'm gonna die...

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:46.510
I'm dying...

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:50.560
You're really going to die if you don't take that thing off, Kayura.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:55.230
I hope you aren't thinking of going back to Tokyo when we just arrived here!

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:57.400
Not at all!

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:02.440
I knew the countryside would be hot!

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:06.820
If you want to live here, you need the wisdom and tact{as in, ability to plan/improvise} to coexist with nature!{countryside used too many times}

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:12.950
So we, too, should {think of ways and }practice living in the countryside!

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:16.710
<i>Wow! Milady said something really smart!</i>

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:21.500
Right then, Hayate. Find a store and buy me some Häagen-Dazs!

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:25.760
Sorry, Nagi, but there aren't any stores around here...

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:29.350
And Starbucks?

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:30.760
Of course not.

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:33.270
<b>Expectations 
for the countryside</b>

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:40.730
<i>This is bad! Her expectations for the countryside are falling like a certain game company's stocks!{what company?}</i>

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:42.610
<i>I have to do something!</i>

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:46.740
Look, Milady! There's a tunnel of trees!

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:50.280
I am certain Totoro's hiding in there!

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:54.700
<b>Expectations 
for the countryside</b>

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:52.410
Seriously, Hayate?!

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:54.700
We must go and find it!

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:57.290
Come on, Chiharu!

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:00.250
We're going to find Totoro!

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:03.250
Hey! Don't pull my arm so hard!

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:04.960
<i>Thank goodness.</i>

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:09.260
<i>Now she might still learn to love the countryside, even if it's a bit hot.</i>

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:10.930
Stupid!

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:12.680
You've never done any sports!

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:14.770
Watch where you're going!{Running around like this could be dangerous!}

00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:17.940
What are you talking about?

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:21.860
If we don't hurry, all the corn will be gone!

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:32.530
A-Are you all right, Milady?

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:35.080
I'm wet.

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:37.040
I'm soaked.

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:39.920
<i>Another rapid drop!</i>

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:44.840
M-Milady, let's get you a bath and a change of clothes!

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:47.170
We'll have some yummy watermelons later!

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:50.510
Are watermelons yummy?

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:55.350
Of course! Watermelons from the countryside are sweet and delicious!

00:06:54.720 --> 00:07:00.190
<b>Expectations 
for the countryside</b>

00:06:57.140 --> 00:06:59.060
<i>It's still pretty low...</i>

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:00.190
I'll have some.

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:02.810
Then let's go!

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:04.900
<i>Hey, Ayasaki.</i>

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:07.900
<i>I fell into the water too, by the way...</i>

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:10.950
Hey! Are you all right?

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:16.740
Even out here, the butler's life is difficult.

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:19.830
Hayate's life is always difficult.

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:29.340
We're here!

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:32.220
Granny! I'm here with the gang!

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:33.970
Good afternoon!

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:40.560
Ah, Ayumu! Welcome, welcome!

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:43.020
I've been waiting for you.

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:49.150
I'm glad you brought so many friends!

00:07:49.150 --> 00:07:56.120
And you've grown up into a beauty! I hardly recognized you at all!

00:07:57.410 --> 00:07:59.250
That's because that's not me!

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:03.210
She's Katsura Hinagiku, my friend!

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:06.130
Granny, where are your glasses?

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:08.090
All right, all right.

00:08:08.590 --> 00:08:13.300
By the way, Granny. Sorry for asking so suddenly, but can we use the bath?

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:15.800
Sure, sure.

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:22.350
Good grief. Having to take a bath as soon as we got here...

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:24.150
It's all because you're so clumsy.

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:25.600
Look who's talking!

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:33.110
When I think about the scorching heat waiting for us when we get out of this bath...

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:35.160
I don't wanna leave.

00:08:35.530 --> 00:08:39.240
You're the one who had such high expectations for this dull place

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:42.120
Don't complain about something so trivial.

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:44.170
That's true, but...

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:49.710
This isn't like a game or anime where you can wait for the fun to come to you.

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:55.090
You won't have any fun out here unless you put some effort into it.

00:08:56.550 --> 00:08:59.060
Put some effort into it?

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:02.270
Like what? Give me an example.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:04.850
Like...

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:10.400
Like! If you ask me...

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:11.900
Why are you coming in?

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:14.450
Like stag beetles!

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:18.280
The stag beetles are gigantic in the countryside!

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:22.660
Stag beetles? Why would a girl be interested in those...

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:25.750
Are they big? Are they really that big?

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:27.880
Are they giraffe stag beetles?

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:29.340
Yes, of course!

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:34.470
The stag beetles around here are just as big as that gira-whatever stag beetle!

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:37.550
Though I've never seen that gira-whatever stag beetle before...

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:42.260
I guess it works if you grew up playing <i>King of the Beetles</i>...

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:48.810
Very well! Then we must go and catch one before someone else does!

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:48.810
<b>Expectations 
for the countryside</b>

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:50.360
Let's go, Chiharu!

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:55.570
Who cares about the bath when giant stag beetles are waiting for us!

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:02.990
What on Earth is the matter, Milady?!

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:08.080
You're wearing weird clothes there, Ayumu.

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:10.920
Is this the new fashion in Tokyo?

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:12.960
Um...

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:20.090
Milady! Shall we go look for Totoro?

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:22.560
I don't care.

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:27.230
I don't... give a damn about Totoro, idiot!

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:28.980
I've had enough!

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:32.060
A spider the size of a dragon  almost killed me!

00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:35.820
I can't go looking for Totoro or stag beetles now!

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:38.900
I'm going to eat this slice of watermelon and go to bed!

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:40.740
Very well.

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:43.530
Then sleep well.

00:10:43.530 --> 00:10:46.750
I'm sure that you'll see it too when you wake up...

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:49.830
All the wonderful things about the countryside.

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:52.880
What are you even talking about...

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:04.050
W-Well, if you insist, I'll think about it...

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:06.970
Thank you very much, Milady.

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:22.320
Hot.

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:37.170
Don't you cicadas have anything else to say?!

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:52.650
Hayate! Hayate, Hayate!

00:11:52.650 --> 00:11:53.690
Coming!

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:56.440
You called, Milady?

00:11:56.440 --> 00:11:57.940
Summer is hot!

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:00.650
The cicadas are bullying me!

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:03.070
And my hands are all sticky!

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:04.450
Do something!

00:12:04.450 --> 00:12:05.700
Do something right now!

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:07.910
I'm not going to last much longer!

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:10.080
It's not going to kill you.

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:13.670
And you shouldn't throw things.

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:15.710
But... But...

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:29.470
All right, now give me your hands.

00:12:29.470 --> 00:12:30.600
I'll wipe them for you.

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:36.230
Oh, my.

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:40.690
Why did you throw that watermelon rind?

00:12:41.240 --> 00:12:43.610
I-It was the only weapon at hand.

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:46.620
But look at how sticky your hands are now.

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:49.030
Sh-Shut up!

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:55.370
Is something the matter, Milady?

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:57.380
Bah! That's enough!

00:13:01.590 --> 00:13:02.800
Geez!

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:06.510
What am I doing in this stupid place?!

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:08.050
Well, we're here to...

00:13:08.550 --> 00:13:12.060
remedy you of being a good-for-nothing, remember?

00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:15.440
Don't call me that!

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:19.900
Can I touch your outstretched hands?

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:22.940
I hold out my fingers, trembling,

00:13:38.540 --> 00:13:41.050
I'm sure this is how it is

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:44.470
I did my best

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:44.420
<b>Good luck, Hayate!</b>

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:50.390
and felt like I was truly alive

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:56.060
I wasn't aiming too high either

00:13:56.850 --> 00:14:02.230
God can be so cruel

00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:07.650
Dreams and reality are both always so chaotic

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:14.330
I still don't know how all this will resolve{*}

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:17.540
I want to embrace with all my strength

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:20.540
the things I can grasp with both my hands

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:23.750
Even if I trip up and stumble, I will be able to laugh again

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:26.550
because you are here for me

00:14:26.550 --> 00:14:29.720
Like the wind that carries the summer warmth

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:32.800
I will breeze through these times

00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:35.100
Now opens up the sky

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:39.020
in which we will fly

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:53.330
Come on, guys! We're not done yet! Here we go!{さぁ、みんな！まだまだいくよ！}

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:04.340
<b>Doujins, Games</b>

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:04.340
<b>Comic</b>

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:04.340
<b>Come on in!</b>

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:02.840
Welcome!{いらっしゃいませ！}

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:07.340
Welcome to Comic V Tachibana, your one-stop shop for doujins and games!{同人誌とゲームの楽園、コミックV タチバナへようこそ！}

00:15:08.720 --> 00:15:09.880
Hey, Saki!{おい、サキ！}

00:15:10.430 --> 00:15:11.590
Man the register!{お前、レジたのむ！}

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:13.600
Okay, I'll be right there!{はい、ただいま！}

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:20.730
Sheesh! Even though NatsuComi was two weeks ago,

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:23.610
this city's still as busy as always.{しかし、夏コミが終わって二週間あまりたつというのに、相変わらず騒がしいな、この街は。}

00:15:23.610 --> 00:15:28.190
Well, all the stores have this year's new goods in stock now.{まぁ、夏コミの再販売が充実してくるときだしね。}

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:29.610
Hey, Kayura.{なぁ、カユラ。}

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:32.610
I know we're in Akiba,{いくら秋葉のろんほ(?)とはいえ、}

00:15:32.610 --> 00:15:35.530
but isn't that cosplay a bit too much?{さすがにそのコスプレはやりすぎではないか？}

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:36.490
Yeah.{ええ、まぁ、そうなんだけど。}

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:38.370
I suppose it is, but...{ええ、まぁ、そうなんだけど。}

00:15:39.710 --> 00:15:42.370
I'm too embarrassed to take it off now.{いまさら恥ずかしくて、脱げない。}

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:44.130
Then don't wear it in the first place!{なら着てくんな！}

00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:55.100
Why can't we have summer vacation all the way until October?

00:15:55.640 --> 00:15:58.850
School starts in just a few days,

00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:02.980
and that makes me depressed about the fleeting summer days gone by.

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:07.230
And even though I'm still young, I've been saddled with so many responsibilities.

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:10.400
I wish I had an easier life.

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:14.200
Kayura? You think so too, don't you, Kayura?

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:16.870
Why don't you go die then?

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:22.580
I can't move an inch.

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:25.210
Am I sick? Gotta be sick.

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:26.250
Right, Kayura?

00:16:26.590 --> 00:16:29.460
By the way, did you buy the new book by Spicy Conspiracy?

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:31.760
I'm already done reading it.

00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:35.890
Is that okay with you, Ayasaki?

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:37.390
What are you talking about?

00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:40.100
Well, I mean...

00:16:40.970 --> 00:16:44.600
I know we were really busy this summer because of NatsuComi,

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:48.480
and I understand she wants to relax now that it's over.

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:52.490
I should've asked Makita for it first...{?}

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:52.490
Still, isn't she...

00:16:52.490 --> 00:16:53.700
That's true.

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:55.950
taking it too far?

00:16:56.820 --> 00:17:02.960
Milady won't <i>really</i> waste the rest of her vacation idling away.

00:17:02.960 --> 00:17:04.290
Are you sure?

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:06.500
There's only a few days until school starts.

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:09.290
If you don't get her out of her slump soon, she's gonna go,

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:12.420
"The second semester is just a fall break between the summer and winter breaks,

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:14.970
so let's just take another break!"

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:17.010
or something like that.

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:20.350
On that note, I've been thinking about fall vacations.

00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:23.230
Don't you think not having a fall vacation in the second semester...

00:17:23.230 --> 00:17:26.400
is kinda like being rude to fall itself?

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:27.600
That's true.

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:29.610
<i>Oh great.</i>

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:31.610
<i>If I don't make her energetic again,</i>

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:33.650
<i>there's no way she'll go to school.</i>

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:39.160
In that case, I might just have...

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:41.580
the perfect idea!

00:17:42.660 --> 00:17:47.080
You want to thank me for your birthday party by inviting me to your vacation home?

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:47.540
Yes!

00:17:48.290 --> 00:17:50.130
That place is really beautiful!

00:17:50.460 --> 00:17:52.170
A lush, green forest!

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:53.960
An enchanting little brook!

00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:55.590
Summer festivals!

00:17:56.430 --> 00:18:00.050
It's a genuine, true-blue Japanese countryside!

00:18:01.430 --> 00:18:03.220
I get it!

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:06.810
If we spend the last days of our vacation surrounded by nature,

00:18:06.810 --> 00:18:10.940
our minds and bodies will be refreshed and ready to face the new semester!

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:14.780
I don't really care to face the new semester though.

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:18.280
Besides, there isn't anything to do out in the boonies, is there?

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:23.080
I don't think you know what the countryside's really like, Nagi.

00:18:24.240 --> 00:18:25.750
Listen closely, Nagi.

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:28.460
It's not that there's <i>nothing</i> to do in the country.

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:33.210
You can <i>do</i> nothing in the country!

00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:34.670
Hey now, just a moment.

00:18:34.670 --> 00:18:37.670
Even if you quote attention-grabbing tidbits from some random manga like that...

00:18:37.670 --> 00:18:39.340
She's actually interested now...

00:18:40.720 --> 00:18:42.510
I can <i>do</i> nothing?

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:44.100
Incredible!

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:46.020
That logic is incredible!

00:18:46.480 --> 00:18:47.640
I see now.

00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:50.480
We were blinded by our folly.

00:18:50.980 --> 00:18:53.360
Even though NatsuComi's already over,

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:55.530
we kept telling ourselves that it was still only the sixth or seventh day.

00:18:55.530 --> 00:18:58.150
We started each day grabbing the newest doujins,{?}

00:18:58.150 --> 00:19:02.240
lurked on 2channel, and patrolled the net until well past 2 AM.

00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:03.740
It was all so shallow!

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:07.250
Indeed, even the Lapita were destroyed when they turned from Mother Earth,

00:19:07.250 --> 00:19:09.210
and said their good-byes to nature.

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:10.870
We must not meet the same fate!

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:15.420
I think we <i>should</i> go to the countryside!

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:16.840
All right!

00:19:16.840 --> 00:19:23.300
Let's go refresh our minds and bodies in paradise doing absolutely nothing!

00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:27.020
You were so bubbly when you said that.

00:19:27.470 --> 00:19:30.560
Why are you so down right after we've arrived?

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:33.230
My iPhone can't get a signal.

00:19:33.610 --> 00:19:34.860
Here!

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:39.440
There's no Animate, no Gamers, no Toranoana{TL Note: Comic Toranoana, check wikipedia}, no Big.

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:41.070
There's nothing but a tiny convenience store!

00:19:41.070 --> 00:19:42.990
There's no Jump on Mondays.

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:46.410
The TV doesn't even get TV Tokyo—just two commercial stations!

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:48.290
There isn't even air conditioning!

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:50.660
Just how "country" is this countryside of yours?!

00:19:50.660 --> 00:19:53.710
Isn't the air so clean and fresh?

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:55.540
Don't say that while sweating!

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:57.960
This was a mistake.

00:19:57.960 --> 00:19:59.050
There's nothing here.

00:19:59.050 --> 00:20:00.550
Seriously, nothing at all!

00:20:00.880 --> 00:20:02.720
It's gonna kill me...

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:04.800
The boredom's gonna kill me!

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:06.300
Oh, come now...

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:08.970
It's all your fault, Hayate!

00:20:08.970 --> 00:20:12.190
"We can refresh our minds and bodies," my foot! Liar!

00:20:12.190 --> 00:20:16.360
And you didn't even let me bring my DS and PSP either!

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:19.650
I didn't really lie.

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:23.450
Besides, I brought a chess set if you want a cha—

00:20:23.450 --> 00:20:26.030
I don't know any other ways to have fun!

00:20:27.030 --> 00:20:30.000
What's with you!? Stupid, stupid Hayate!

00:20:30.620 --> 00:20:31.500
Hmph!

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:40.550
Milady! At least give it a shot! It might be more fun than you think!

00:20:35.830 --> 00:20:40.260
The job of a butler's never easy...

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:44.220
On the other hand, those two look like they're having fun.

00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:49.850
Did you know an ant releases a pheromone trail when it finds food?

00:20:49.850 --> 00:20:56.100
Then, the other ants follow that trail to find the food and help carry it back.

00:20:56.100 --> 00:21:00.110
So if you remove a part of the trail...

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:04.610
They can't follow the scent and fall into chaos!

00:21:04.610 --> 00:21:06.870
Goodness! How devious!

00:21:06.870 --> 00:21:08.200
You fiend!

00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:11.830
Mother Earth won't forgive you for mistreating her children so, Risa!

00:21:13.410 --> 00:21:16.290
And what have I to be afraid of, Mikki?

00:21:17.880 --> 00:21:18.880
It's obvious.

00:21:19.540 --> 00:21:22.380
Bang! Water cannon!

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:26.720
Stop it! Stop! I'm all wet now!

00:21:27.800 --> 00:21:28.720
Do you see?

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:30.470
Fear the wrath of the planet!

00:21:31.100 --> 00:21:32.470
Wow!

00:21:32.470 --> 00:21:34.480
Such big sunflowers!

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:37.980
We cultivated them to grow them this big.

00:21:38.480 --> 00:21:41.480
They're really, really pretty!

00:21:41.730 --> 00:21:43.990
Yeah! They are!

00:21:44.740 --> 00:21:46.660
They're just gonna wither away.

00:21:47.200 --> 00:21:49.530
Why do they even bother?

00:21:50.530 --> 00:21:51.580
Umm...

00:21:52.410 --> 00:21:55.910
That's kinda hard to answer.

00:21:55.910 --> 00:21:58.630
Maybe the flowers want to bloom their very best while they still can—

00:21:58.630 --> 00:21:59.750
Girls! Look!

00:22:02.420 --> 00:22:04.970
They gave out so many sunflowers!

00:22:04.970 --> 00:22:08.680
Here's to the one who dares enter the stage like that!

00:22:09.300 --> 00:22:10.890
Blow her away!

00:22:11.510 --> 00:22:13.310
What are you doing?!

00:22:13.310 --> 00:22:15.020
I'm getting drenched!

00:22:15.020 --> 00:22:16.270
Silence, whelp!

00:22:16.270 --> 00:22:18.020
Such is the punishment for betraying us!

00:22:18.020 --> 00:22:19.520
Mow the weed!

00:22:20.730 --> 00:22:22.900
Stop being mean, you two!

00:22:23.650 --> 00:22:25.530
Good! Finish her!

00:22:26.030 --> 00:22:28.530
Huh? It... stopped.

00:22:31.030 --> 00:22:32.410
But why?

00:22:36.660 --> 00:22:38.370
Good grief!

00:22:38.370 --> 00:22:40.330
Stop playing with water!

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:42.840
You're all drenched now!

00:22:41.330 --> 00:22:44.300
Hina! Thanks!

00:22:42.840 --> 00:22:44.300
So are you!

00:22:45.590 --> 00:22:47.920
How do you like the countryside, Hina?

00:22:51.430 --> 00:22:54.680
It's really beautiful.

00:22:56.100 --> 00:22:57.930
Thank you!

00:22:57.930 --> 00:23:00.600
The summer festival the day after tomorrow will be fun too!

00:23:00.600 --> 00:23:03.190
It's a festival for a local god,

00:23:03.570 --> 00:23:07.610
who's said to be able to make one of your feelings come true.

00:23:08.320 --> 00:23:11.570
Not a wish, but a feeling?

00:23:11.910 --> 00:23:14.370
Isn't it romantic?

00:23:15.330 --> 00:23:16.830
Sure is.

00:23:21.710 --> 00:23:24.840
How much longer do I have to do nothing?

00:23:24.840 --> 00:23:27.260
What's going to happen to me?

00:23:27.260 --> 00:23:30.970
Come on, Milady, stop talking like that.

00:23:30.970 --> 00:23:35.350
There are so many things here that you can't find in Akihabara!

00:23:35.350 --> 00:23:37.720
What, are they selling a new PSP here?

00:23:37.970 --> 00:23:42.560
You would actually be surprised...

00:23:42.560 --> 00:23:44.190
But I don't mean that.

00:23:48.070 --> 00:23:51.490
Look over there! The sun is so high in the sky—

00:24:04.920 --> 00:24:06.250
Hayate?

00:24:07.840 --> 00:24:09.210
Is something wrong?

00:24:09.210 --> 00:24:11.420
No, I just...

00:24:11.420 --> 00:24:13.090
saw someone over there who I'd never seen before—

00:24:14.140 --> 00:24:15.050
Huh?

00:24:15.050 --> 00:24:16.930
There's no one there.

00:24:18.850 --> 00:24:20.180
Did you imagine it?

00:24:20.730 --> 00:24:22.850
But I'm sure I...

00:24:23.190 --> 00:24:24.190
Told you!

00:24:24.190 --> 00:24:26.980
The boredom's getting to your head!

00:24:26.980 --> 00:24:30.440
It's true that man cannot live where there's no iPhone signal.

00:24:30.440 --> 00:24:33.150
No, it's not like that.

00:24:33.950 --> 00:24:35.530
Right then, let's go home.

00:24:36.070 --> 00:24:38.580
W-Wait a second, Milady!

00:24:38.580 --> 00:24:44.080
For me, the world is the cell phone coverage area!

00:24:44.080 --> 00:24:46.580
That hurts, Milady!

00:24:46.580 --> 00:24:50.300
Being a butler sure is hard work...

00:24:50.300 --> 00:24:51.760
Indeed it is.

00:25:17.700 --> 00:25:18.950
It was...

00:25:18.950 --> 00:25:20.370
as the ancients called it...

00:25:20.370 --> 00:25:23.200
the "witching hour".

00:25:23.830 --> 00:25:26.620
Dank air filled the room...

00:25:27.540 --> 00:25:30.420
Something dripped...

00:25:30.420 --> 00:25:33.130
and dripped from the ceiling.

00:25:37.050 --> 00:25:41.560
And as the girl lay unaware,

00:25:41.560 --> 00:25:44.060
a dark, shadowy haze appeared behind her.

00:25:46.230 --> 00:25:48.480
When she turned to look at it,

00:25:49.150 --> 00:25:52.360
it slowly took human form.

00:25:52.980 --> 00:25:54.530
And suddenly—

00:26:03.080 --> 00:26:07.790
The next day, there was a bloody spectacle on that very spot.

00:26:11.340 --> 00:26:14.380
Man! Talk about spending summer in the country!

00:26:14.380 --> 00:26:16.470
This really gets me on!

00:26:16.470 --> 00:26:19.260
Yeah, this is an important part of the process.

00:26:20.100 --> 00:26:23.520
By the way, you wanna do a test of courage after this?

00:26:23.520 --> 00:26:25.680
Oh! Good idea!

00:26:25.680 --> 00:26:28.600
I-I'm not going!

00:26:34.480 --> 00:26:35.650
That sucked.

00:26:36.070 --> 00:26:37.570
So bathrooms in the country...

00:26:38.240 --> 00:26:39.910
don't have locks.

00:26:42.620 --> 00:26:44.040
Still...

00:26:47.580 --> 00:26:49.620
<i>It still bugs me.</i>

00:26:49.620 --> 00:26:52.960
<i>And I'm sure she said something back then.</i>

00:26:53.670 --> 00:26:55.380
<i>I'll save you.</i>

00:27:14.820 --> 00:27:17.440
E-Excuse me, I want to go use the restroom...

00:27:19.490 --> 00:27:22.320
No, that's not what I meant.

00:27:22.320 --> 00:27:24.160
Maria, restroom...

00:27:33.130 --> 00:27:34.920
I... I'm fine on my own—

00:27:47.180 --> 00:27:49.680
Ha... Hayate!

00:27:49.680 --> 00:27:51.940
What is it, Milady?

00:27:54.110 --> 00:27:56.360
Ha... Hayate?

00:27:58.230 --> 00:27:59.900
Don't scare me like that!

00:27:59.900 --> 00:28:02.410
What are you doing here in the middle of the night?

00:28:02.910 --> 00:28:04.530
I'm sorry.

00:28:04.530 --> 00:28:07.450
I was trying to find a place with a signal.

00:28:07.870 --> 00:28:11.160
I finally got it on the tall hill outside the village.

00:28:12.000 --> 00:28:16.460
You sure can walk around in the dark just fine, can't you?

00:28:16.750 --> 00:28:17.750
Dark?

00:28:17.750 --> 00:28:18.920
Of course!

00:28:18.920 --> 00:28:22.970
The streets in Tokyo are lit up through the night.

00:28:22.970 --> 00:28:25.220
It's bright here in the country too.

00:28:25.680 --> 00:28:27.720
Come with me, Milady.

00:28:28.970 --> 00:28:30.480
Hayate?

00:28:39.900 --> 00:28:40.820
Look!

00:28:47.660 --> 00:28:50.370
Sure, the night sky in Mykonos was pretty,

00:28:50.370 --> 00:28:52.830
but the sky in Japan isn't too shabby either, is it?

00:29:00.460 --> 00:29:04.260
Hayate, there's something I want you to do.

00:29:04.720 --> 00:29:07.100
Is it urgent? It's the middle of the night...

00:29:07.100 --> 00:29:11.020
Well, kinda. I...

00:29:16.270 --> 00:29:18.610
You! From earlier!

00:29:24.610 --> 00:29:26.110
Wait!

00:29:26.110 --> 00:29:26.820
Hayate?

00:29:28.070 --> 00:29:29.870
Please excuse me, Milady.

00:29:29.870 --> 00:29:31.830
I'll listen to your request in the morning.

00:29:31.830 --> 00:29:33.330
Please go to bed now.

00:29:33.330 --> 00:29:35.830
I'm going to chase after that woman.

00:29:35.830 --> 00:29:39.130
I <i>can't</i> wait till morning!

00:29:39.130 --> 00:29:40.090
I...

00:29:40.090 --> 00:29:42.590
Wait! Who's this woman you're talking about?

00:29:42.590 --> 00:29:45.880
Hey! Like I said...

00:29:50.970 --> 00:29:54.230
H-H-Hayate! Wait for me!

00:30:00.400 --> 00:30:02.650
<i>Who was that woman?</i>

00:30:02.650 --> 00:30:05.780
<i>I feel like I've seen her...</i>

00:30:06.650 --> 00:30:08.660
<i>I've seen her before.</i>

00:30:24.130 --> 00:30:25.470
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:30:26.760 --> 00:30:27.840
<i>What's this?!</i>

00:30:43.900 --> 00:30:45.940
<i>There was an amusement park here?</i>

00:30:48.950 --> 00:30:55.040
<i>But I feel like... I've been here before...</i>

00:31:00.080 --> 00:31:01.920
This is awesome!

00:31:03.540 --> 00:31:04.670
It really is.

00:31:04.670 --> 00:31:07.220
Pretty cool for the boonies.

00:31:08.760 --> 00:31:11.340
What are you girls doing here?

00:31:11.340 --> 00:31:13.550
Obviously, we're having a test of courage.

00:31:13.550 --> 00:31:16.060
We stayed up too late and then couldn't fall asleep.

00:31:16.060 --> 00:31:19.350
Look, look! These two are so cute!

00:31:19.350 --> 00:31:21.310
There's a roller coaster over there.

00:31:21.310 --> 00:31:22.440
Wow, I wanna ride!

00:31:23.360 --> 00:31:27.400
W-Wait up! We don't know if it's safe—

00:31:27.400 --> 00:31:30.700
Hayata, these crepes are delicious!

00:31:34.160 --> 00:31:37.450
Hayata, hurry!

00:31:37.450 --> 00:31:40.920
Just how adaptable are these girls?{eg they can adapt quick}

00:31:43.290 --> 00:31:44.880
That sounded like Milady!

00:31:45.210 --> 00:31:47.920
What the heck are you?!

00:31:52.300 --> 00:31:53.590
Milady!

00:31:53.590 --> 00:31:54.350
Hayate!

00:31:54.350 --> 00:31:56.430
What do you think you're doing to Milady?!

00:31:56.430 --> 00:31:58.060
Hayate!

00:32:00.520 --> 00:32:01.520
Stop!

00:32:01.940 --> 00:32:03.440
Hayate!

00:32:05.230 --> 00:32:06.650
Milady!

00:32:37.930 --> 00:32:39.180
Milady!

00:32:39.720 --> 00:32:40.930
Milady!

00:32:41.890 --> 00:32:43.100
Milady!

00:32:44.190 --> 00:32:46.110
What's wrong, Hayate?

00:32:46.110 --> 00:32:48.770
I'm sorry. Where's Milady?

00:32:48.770 --> 00:32:50.940
She's right there.

00:32:57.070 --> 00:32:58.830
Good morning, Hayate.

00:33:09.170 --> 00:33:11.630
Good morning, Milady.

00:33:13.630 --> 00:33:15.930
You look like you came here in a hurry.

00:33:15.930 --> 00:33:17.800
Is everything all right?

00:33:17.800 --> 00:33:19.100
Ah, no.

00:33:19.680 --> 00:33:22.310
Did you have a scary nightmare?

00:33:22.310 --> 00:33:23.600
Oh, is that true?

00:33:26.350 --> 00:33:28.440
I guess... I did.

00:33:29.070 --> 00:33:31.610
<i>I guess it was all a dream.</i>

00:33:32.940 --> 00:33:36.240
Morning! Looks like it'll be a sauna again.

00:33:36.240 --> 00:33:40.280
It does! How about a riverside barbeque?

00:33:40.280 --> 00:33:42.370
That sounds great.

00:33:42.370 --> 00:33:45.670
Hey, forget that. Remember when I said...

00:33:43.960 --> 00:33:46.620
So, what kind of nightmare was it?

00:33:47.250 --> 00:33:49.630
Umm, I saw...

00:33:54.760 --> 00:33:57.050
I can't really remember it now.

00:34:03.140 --> 00:34:05.310
We can't get out from here either.

00:34:05.980 --> 00:34:09.150
There's a weird barrier holding me back.

00:34:09.610 --> 00:34:11.020
A closed space.

00:34:11.020 --> 00:34:13.110
We're in a closed space, right?

00:34:13.110 --> 00:34:15.440
This isn't the time to get excited!{This isn't the time to be a weaboo!}

00:34:15.440 --> 00:34:17.660
And put that uniform away!

00:34:18.450 --> 00:34:19.910
This isn't good.

00:34:20.280 --> 00:34:23.490
This might be a global crisis.

00:34:24.160 --> 00:34:26.160
Is Hayate all right?

00:34:26.160 --> 00:34:30.590
The whole world might end soon if I don't find that woman and get out.

00:34:31.040 --> 00:34:32.590
Here, Nagi. Have my crepe.

00:34:32.590 --> 00:34:34.340
It's really delicious!

00:34:34.340 --> 00:34:37.380
Nagi, that roller coaster's so cool!

00:34:37.380 --> 00:34:40.550
Hey, why are you all messing around?!

00:34:41.260 --> 00:34:43.510
But the crepe really is delicious.

00:34:43.510 --> 00:34:46.020
And you can ride the rollercoaster as much as you want.

00:34:46.020 --> 00:34:48.060
That doesn't matter!

00:34:48.060 --> 00:34:52.400
We're in an empty amusement park in the middle of nowhere and we can't get out!

00:34:52.400 --> 00:34:55.860
Don't you find something strange about our situation?

00:34:57.900 --> 00:34:58.950
What?

00:34:59.530 --> 00:35:01.280
Restroom.

00:35:01.280 --> 00:35:02.580
That way.

00:35:16.800 --> 00:35:17.970
Eat this!

00:35:20.050 --> 00:35:21.590
Hey!

00:35:23.260 --> 00:35:24.560
Take that!

00:35:26.350 --> 00:35:28.310
This feels great!

00:35:28.310 --> 00:35:30.230
Here you go, Hayate.

00:35:30.730 --> 00:35:32.440
I grilled them myself.

00:35:33.940 --> 00:35:37.190
Thank you, Milady.

00:35:38.900 --> 00:35:40.110
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:35:40.110 --> 00:35:45.490
<i>I'm having fun, but I feel like I'm forgetting something important.</i>

00:35:45.490 --> 00:35:46.910
<i>Really important...</i>

00:35:48.790 --> 00:35:51.750
I'm almost done with everyone else's, okay?

00:35:51.750 --> 00:35:54.750
Milady! What are you doing?!

00:35:55.170 --> 00:35:58.130
You don't have to do it yourself, Milady!

00:35:58.130 --> 00:36:01.300
Just lie down under the parasol and smile!

00:36:01.930 --> 00:36:03.510
You're right.

00:36:03.970 --> 00:36:06.470
What was that all about? My body just...

00:36:06.470 --> 00:36:09.770
I just started doing the chores.

00:36:09.770 --> 00:36:12.520
You don't have to do the chores, Milady.

00:36:13.980 --> 00:36:18.440
Come, have a seat in the shade and let me do the rest.

00:36:19.070 --> 00:36:19.990
Okay.

00:36:23.740 --> 00:36:28.540
<i>Not good. Milady did that because I was daydreaming.</i>

00:36:28.990 --> 00:36:32.670
<i>But what is it I'm forgetting..?</i>

00:36:33.670 --> 00:36:34.920
Milady!

00:36:34.920 --> 00:36:37.920
I-I'm sorry! My body was moving on its own...

00:36:39.260 --> 00:36:43.010
Just what <i>is</i> this place?

00:36:44.050 --> 00:36:47.300
That looks good on you, Nagi!

00:36:48.560 --> 00:36:52.060
I didn't have anything but my pajamas! I had no choice!

00:36:53.230 --> 00:36:56.480
I want to wear one too!

00:36:56.480 --> 00:37:00.320
Just how can you all be so optimistic?

00:37:00.780 --> 00:37:05.070
So much time has passed since we came here, but it's still night.

00:37:05.070 --> 00:37:06.950
And I just noticed—there's no moon either!

00:37:06.950 --> 00:37:09.950
We can't even get out of here!

00:37:10.290 --> 00:37:11.950
We can't?

00:37:11.950 --> 00:37:12.870
Really?

00:37:12.870 --> 00:37:15.880
I've been saying that all along!

00:37:17.210 --> 00:37:21.590
So, could this be a you-know-what?

00:37:21.590 --> 00:37:23.720
Have we been spirited away?

00:37:23.720 --> 00:37:25.590
Spirited away?

00:37:25.590 --> 00:37:29.560
I see... So you're saying this time,

00:37:32.060 --> 00:37:33.230
<i>we</i> were the ones spirited away!

00:37:35.690 --> 00:37:37.900
Oh no! What are going to do?!

00:37:37.900 --> 00:37:39.730
Don't start panicking <i>now</i>!

00:37:39.730 --> 00:37:42.570
Somebody help!

00:37:48.070 --> 00:37:51.990
Sheesh! I really want more money, ya hear?

00:37:52.410 --> 00:37:55.250
We're at the school pool. Drop the act.

00:37:55.710 --> 00:37:59.040
Why didn't you go with Hinagiku on their trip?

00:37:59.040 --> 00:38:04.510
I refuse to spend the rest of my holiday in some Japanese country shithole.

00:38:04.880 --> 00:38:10.050
Summer is for passing the time at the school pool where I can get in for free.

00:38:10.930 --> 00:38:13.390
"Buried Treasures in the Japanese countryside"

00:38:15.890 --> 00:38:20.190
"In the village, they hold an annual festival that fulfills one's feelings,

00:38:20.190 --> 00:38:25.610
but this tradition comes from nothing but a legend of a diamond!"

00:38:25.610 --> 00:38:28.950
"This diamond, still believed to be buried somewhere in the forest,

00:38:28.950 --> 00:38:33.160
"is worth, if the legends are to be believed, up to 100-150 million..."

00:38:33.540 --> 00:38:34.910
Diamond?

00:38:39.920 --> 00:38:42.000
Told ya summer should be in the country!

00:38:42.000 --> 00:38:43.550
You change your mind too quickly!

00:38:43.550 --> 00:38:47.300
Don't forget, I really love this car, so be careful, okay?

00:38:47.300 --> 00:38:49.470
Don't you dare scratch it!

00:38:49.470 --> 00:38:52.010
It'll be okay! It's insured, isn't it?

00:38:52.010 --> 00:38:53.430
You're going to smash it to bits, aren't you?!

00:39:01.480 --> 00:39:05.320
Girls! The barbecue's ready!

00:39:05.900 --> 00:39:07.360
Coming!

00:39:10.950 --> 00:39:13.660
Meat tastes great outdoors!

00:39:13.660 --> 00:39:14.580
It really does.

00:39:17.660 --> 00:39:19.210
Isn't this fun, Hayate?

00:39:20.670 --> 00:39:22.080
It really is!

00:39:22.840 --> 00:39:24.340
<i>That's right, it really is.</i>

00:39:24.340 --> 00:39:27.090
<i>But... there's something...</i>

00:39:27.090 --> 00:39:28.220
Here!

00:39:28.220 --> 00:39:30.180
Don't just stand there cooking all day.

00:39:30.180 --> 00:39:30.970
Eat some yourself.

00:39:32.050 --> 00:39:33.970
Sure! Thank you.

00:39:34.430 --> 00:39:37.020
<i>I'm forgetting something.</i>

00:39:37.020 --> 00:39:39.100
<i>Something important...</i>

00:39:39.100 --> 00:39:41.190
Umm, Hayate?

00:39:41.190 --> 00:39:41.730
Yes?

00:39:42.190 --> 00:39:44.730
Wanna let go?

00:39:46.610 --> 00:39:49.490
Oh geez, I'm sorry, Hinagiku!

00:39:49.490 --> 00:39:51.780
Hey, what's gotten into you?

00:39:51.780 --> 00:39:55.370
Holding my hand out of the blue...

00:39:55.780 --> 00:39:56.620
<i>Hand?</i>

00:40:00.410 --> 00:40:02.040
<i>I just remembered...</i>

00:40:03.250 --> 00:40:04.250
Hayate?

00:40:06.340 --> 00:40:09.550
<i>I just remembered... something important...</i>

00:40:10.340 --> 00:40:11.550
<i>That was...</i>

00:40:16.140 --> 00:40:17.850
Excuse me, Hinagiku.

00:40:17.850 --> 00:40:19.810
Can you come with me for a sec?

00:40:20.390 --> 00:40:21.390
Please!

00:40:21.770 --> 00:40:23.190
W-What?

00:40:31.450 --> 00:40:34.070
There's really no way out!

00:40:34.070 --> 00:40:38.040
Risa! This is happening because you messed with those ants!

00:40:38.040 --> 00:40:42.410
If ants had the power to spirit people away, humanity would be done for!

00:40:42.410 --> 00:40:45.790
Come on, calm down, you three.

00:40:45.790 --> 00:40:48.210
Don't act superior to your seniors!

00:40:48.210 --> 00:40:49.130
Shut up!

00:40:49.130 --> 00:40:52.880
We have to put our heads together to figure a way out!

00:40:52.880 --> 00:40:54.260
Nagi...

00:40:54.260 --> 00:40:56.220
Then I guess we have to do this first.

00:40:56.220 --> 00:40:58.640
We just need to call the police or the national guard—

00:40:58.640 --> 00:41:01.390
Your battery's dead

00:40:58.640 --> 00:41:01.390
<b>silly!</b>

00:41:01.390 --> 00:41:05.810
My battery's dead! I was babbling away for too long!

00:41:05.810 --> 00:41:08.070
Dammit! Mine's dead too!

00:41:08.070 --> 00:41:10.150
Just how freaked out are you lot?

00:41:11.070 --> 00:41:14.780
Maybe we can get reception inside this closed space after all.

00:41:14.780 --> 00:41:15.780
Really?

00:41:16.910 --> 00:41:19.540
I think I saw the bar flicker for an instant.

00:41:19.540 --> 00:41:21.160
But it's probably impossible.

00:41:21.160 --> 00:41:24.750
We're in a forest in the middle of the country.

00:41:24.750 --> 00:41:26.380
There's no way we'll get a signal.

00:41:26.380 --> 00:41:27.330
Dammit...

00:41:27.330 --> 00:41:30.300
All right! We're just going to have to use Power Level Theory!

00:41:31.340 --> 00:41:32.760
Power what?

00:41:33.220 --> 00:41:36.550
One cell phone is one thousand power!{TL Note: The original is http://d.hatena.ne.jp/keyword/%A5%A6%A5%A9%A1%BC%A5%BA%A5%DE%A5%F3%CD%FD%CF%C0 which uses different numbers. Deal with it.}

00:41:36.550 --> 00:41:41.390
That means two is two thousand power!

00:41:41.390 --> 00:41:44.230
And then if you jump twice as high,

00:41:44.230 --> 00:41:46.730
that doubles the power to four thousand power!

00:41:46.730 --> 00:41:51.360
Then, if you spin three times more—that's three times four—

00:41:51.780 --> 00:41:53.650
you'll be over nine thousand!

00:41:53.650 --> 00:41:56.950
Twelve thousand power!

00:42:01.240 --> 00:42:03.540
Zero multiplied by anything is still zero though.

00:42:03.540 --> 00:42:07.540
Let's leave that idiot to herself and find a place with a signal.

00:42:07.540 --> 00:42:08.790
Yeah.

00:42:09.670 --> 00:42:11.630
A place with a signal, huh?

00:42:12.000 --> 00:42:14.090
I finally got it on the tall hill outside the village.

00:42:14.720 --> 00:42:17.300
That's it! We need a high place!

00:42:20.180 --> 00:42:21.310
Over there!

00:42:31.270 --> 00:42:33.110
<i>That's right. It happened here.</i>

00:42:33.570 --> 00:42:35.240
W-What are you doing?

00:42:35.240 --> 00:42:37.910
Why did you bring me... to this empty room?

00:42:37.910 --> 00:42:39.450
Pardon me, Hinagiku.

00:42:39.910 --> 00:42:41.450
Come here for a sec.

00:42:41.450 --> 00:42:42.330
Huh?

00:42:48.420 --> 00:42:50.920
<i>This is it! This sensation.</i>

00:42:51.630 --> 00:42:55.630
<i>I've felt this sensation... somewhere.</i>

00:42:59.720 --> 00:43:01.640
Dammit! It's not enough!

00:43:04.430 --> 00:43:06.310
I'm sorry, Hinagiku.

00:43:06.310 --> 00:43:08.270
I was mistaken.

00:43:11.900 --> 00:43:14.230
What exactly are you sorry about?!

00:43:14.230 --> 00:43:15.280
Sheesh!

00:43:20.110 --> 00:43:24.490
<i>What is this... this feeling of dread in my chest?</i>

00:43:24.490 --> 00:43:25.580
Hayate?

00:43:30.370 --> 00:43:31.330
Hayate?

00:43:35.380 --> 00:43:36.510
You...

00:43:43.890 --> 00:43:45.390
<i>Gosh...</i>

00:43:45.390 --> 00:43:50.230
<i>First, he drags me all the way there, then he ditches me.</i>

00:43:50.850 --> 00:43:52.850
<i>What's going on in his head?!</i>

00:43:56.730 --> 00:43:59.650
Hayate, you're an idiot!

00:44:00.490 --> 00:44:04.700
I'm never going to help you again!

00:44:06.080 --> 00:44:09.660
What, he's breaking hearts all the way out here in the country?

00:44:09.660 --> 00:44:11.580
Oh, that broke butler.

00:44:12.000 --> 00:44:13.880
Well done, Hayate.

00:44:13.880 --> 00:44:17.250
I-I'm not having a lover's quarrel with him!

00:44:17.250 --> 00:44:21.680
All this will come back to that broke butler some day.

00:44:21.680 --> 00:44:27.140
Yes, the student council president will beat him into jelly.

00:44:27.140 --> 00:44:29.850
I'm not going to do that!

00:44:31.270 --> 00:44:34.560
Wait, why are you two here?

00:44:36.270 --> 00:44:39.230
I don't really know myself.

00:44:39.230 --> 00:44:42.280
I received a phone call from Hayate last night.

00:44:42.650 --> 00:44:45.160
He seemed a bit worried.

00:44:45.910 --> 00:44:48.950
You by yourself, Prez?

00:44:48.950 --> 00:44:51.160
Where are Nagi and the others?

00:44:52.410 --> 00:44:53.920
Nagi?

00:44:54.460 --> 00:44:56.040
That's the first time I've heard that name.

00:44:57.710 --> 00:44:59.920
Hey now, President.

00:44:59.920 --> 00:45:01.050
What did you just say?

00:45:02.130 --> 00:45:05.510
Like I said, this is the first time I've heard that name.

00:45:09.140 --> 00:45:10.390
I see.

00:45:10.390 --> 00:45:13.690
I'm beginning to understand why I was called here.

00:45:22.190 --> 00:45:26.740
We might be able to get a signal at the top of this Ferris wheel.

00:45:26.740 --> 00:45:27.950
I see.

00:45:27.950 --> 00:45:31.200
Nagi's iPhone is the only cell phone left!

00:45:31.200 --> 00:45:33.250
Now, like a shounen manga!

00:45:33.250 --> 00:45:35.920
Infuse the scene with friendship, perseverance, and victory!

00:45:35.920 --> 00:45:38.590
Let's all work together for our success!

00:45:39.170 --> 00:45:40.000
Let's go!

00:45:41.250 --> 00:45:44.420
I'll be the staff who opens the gate for the customers.

00:45:44.420 --> 00:45:48.550
Then I'll be the lady who guides the customers to the ride!

00:45:48.550 --> 00:45:54.020
And I'll be the customer who's waiting in the line all alone!

00:45:54.020 --> 00:45:56.190
Just get in the damn car!

00:45:58.520 --> 00:46:00.520
Well, all right, but...

00:46:00.520 --> 00:46:05.150
We can't play here anymore if we call for help.

00:46:05.150 --> 00:46:06.530
Are you idiots?!

00:46:06.530 --> 00:46:09.910
You still want to have fun after everything that's happened?!

00:46:09.910 --> 00:46:13.290
B-But I haven't even tried those rides yet.

00:46:13.290 --> 00:46:18.250
What about the brilliant infusion of friendship, perseverance and victory?!

00:46:18.880 --> 00:46:20.040
It's okay.

00:46:20.960 --> 00:46:22.550
I'll come.

00:46:22.550 --> 00:46:24.420
Together, to the top.

00:46:26.680 --> 00:46:27.680
Kayura!

00:46:29.140 --> 00:46:32.510
A friend in need really is a friend indeed!

00:46:34.060 --> 00:46:35.810
Yeah. You better lick my boots later.{lit. be so grateful that you die}

00:46:39.730 --> 00:46:42.730
Weird. This door doesn't shut.

00:46:42.730 --> 00:46:44.480
Is it broken?

00:46:45.110 --> 00:46:46.280
Looks like it.

00:46:51.160 --> 00:46:53.660
Ah. It gets locked from the outside.

00:46:54.120 --> 00:46:55.870
It wasn't broken.

00:46:55.870 --> 00:46:57.250
I see.

00:47:06.210 --> 00:47:09.590
Farewell, <i>my friend</i>.

00:47:10.760 --> 00:47:12.800
You moron!

00:47:13.850 --> 00:47:14.970
Bah! Whatever!

00:47:16.850 --> 00:47:20.150
No signal

00:47:17.640 --> 00:47:19.850
<i>If I can just get a signal,</i>

00:47:20.440 --> 00:47:21.900
<i>then Hayate will surely...</i>

00:47:22.730 --> 00:47:25.400
<i>Hayate will surely come to save me.</i>

00:47:27.070 --> 00:47:31.410
So, do you really believe that treasure exists?

00:47:31.410 --> 00:47:32.660
Of course!

00:47:32.660 --> 00:47:35.410
My world history teacher's eyes know a treasure when they see it!

00:47:36.910 --> 00:47:40.750
They seem to be quite blinded right now.

00:47:42.170 --> 00:47:46.050
Buried treasure

00:47:42.170 --> 00:47:46.050
FOUND!!

00:47:42.170 --> 00:47:46.050
The village where the treasure
 is thought to be buried

00:47:42.960 --> 00:47:46.050
Besides, someone else already found the treasure.

00:47:47.010 --> 00:47:50.130
Oh! You're right. We've gotta hurry!

00:47:50.130 --> 00:47:51.550
I know a shortcut!

00:47:54.260 --> 00:47:56.680
You idiot! What are you doing?!

00:47:56.680 --> 00:47:59.270
This way is faster to the goal!

00:47:59.270 --> 00:48:02.440
But going in a straight line is stupid!

00:48:09.990 --> 00:48:12.530
You moron!

00:48:10.450 --> 00:48:12.530
My treasure!

00:48:22.540 --> 00:48:25.590
Why are you working as a butler, Hayate?

00:48:26.420 --> 00:48:27.670
Why?

00:48:28.210 --> 00:48:30.670
That's because...

00:48:30.670 --> 00:48:33.130
Good luck, Hayate!

00:48:31.590 --> 00:48:35.300
My parents left me with a debt of 150 million yen,

00:48:35.300 --> 00:48:38.640
and Milady took care of that debt for me.

00:48:39.640 --> 00:48:41.020
Something like that.

00:48:42.140 --> 00:48:44.270
Oh? Then...

00:48:45.560 --> 00:48:46.940
Then take this.

00:48:50.990 --> 00:48:51.990
What is this?

00:48:52.610 --> 00:48:55.870
It's a diamond I had found and kept hidden.

00:48:56.320 --> 00:49:00.450
I'm sure you can get more than 150 million yen if you sell it.

00:49:02.120 --> 00:49:05.330
No! I can't sell something so valuable!

00:49:05.750 --> 00:49:08.300
No, you <i>can</i>.

00:49:08.840 --> 00:49:11.090
You have the <i>right</i> to sell it.

00:49:12.010 --> 00:49:13.090
Right?

00:49:13.720 --> 00:49:16.600
You will no longer be confined in a cage of money.

00:49:17.050 --> 00:49:18.970
You can live as you please, do as you please.

00:49:18.970 --> 00:49:23.640
You won't have to take care of that neglected girl any longer.

00:49:23.640 --> 00:49:25.310
B-But...

00:49:25.730 --> 00:49:26.650
I...

00:49:27.230 --> 00:49:29.190
I can't just forget about her.

00:49:30.230 --> 00:49:31.230
I see.

00:49:31.780 --> 00:49:34.740
If I can't convince you to do it,

00:49:36.110 --> 00:49:38.870
then I'll just have to make you.

00:49:44.120 --> 00:49:45.500
Wait!

00:49:45.500 --> 00:49:46.750
Stop!

00:49:47.960 --> 00:49:49.500
Please, stop!

00:49:49.960 --> 00:49:51.760
Hold it!

00:49:56.050 --> 00:49:59.100
What are you doing, Milady?

00:50:00.060 --> 00:50:01.930
U-Umm...

00:50:02.640 --> 00:50:04.850
It's not what you think!

00:50:04.850 --> 00:50:06.850
I-I'm just...

00:50:06.850 --> 00:50:13.110
I was just wondering what you and Hinagiku were doing together, so...

00:50:15.110 --> 00:50:19.120
You feel like you've been forgetting something too, don't you, Hayate?

00:50:25.870 --> 00:50:28.540
I feel so too.

00:50:29.330 --> 00:50:30.340
That's why...

00:50:31.210 --> 00:50:32.460
Milady?

00:50:33.880 --> 00:50:40.640
I think it was something... something like this.

00:50:40.640 --> 00:50:44.100
Something round and sweet.

00:50:44.100 --> 00:50:46.020
Was it?

00:50:47.140 --> 00:50:48.230
Oh!

00:50:48.230 --> 00:50:50.020
Did you remember?

00:50:50.020 --> 00:50:51.230
Watermelon!

00:50:51.230 --> 00:50:53.150
It must be watermelon!

00:50:53.150 --> 00:50:54.190
Watermelon!

00:50:54.190 --> 00:50:55.530
It's round and sweet!

00:50:55.530 --> 00:50:56.740
Huh?

00:50:56.740 --> 00:50:58.820
Was that it?

00:50:58.820 --> 00:51:01.200
I think we have some left, too.

00:51:01.200 --> 00:51:02.780
I'll go cut some!

00:51:02.780 --> 00:51:06.710
I keep telling you that you don't need to do that!

00:51:06.710 --> 00:51:10.170
Leave all the chores to me!

00:51:10.170 --> 00:51:11.250
Milady?

00:51:11.250 --> 00:51:13.000
Milady!

00:51:19.430 --> 00:51:21.970
What happened? It stopped!

00:51:23.470 --> 00:51:26.980
Damn. There's no signal yet.

00:51:24.060 --> 00:51:27.680
No signal

00:51:28.180 --> 00:51:29.390
Hayate...

00:51:29.390 --> 00:51:31.150
Hayate won't come.

00:51:32.110 --> 00:51:34.190
Y-Y-You're...?!

00:51:35.940 --> 00:51:37.400
Hayate won't come.

00:51:37.400 --> 00:51:38.070
What?

00:51:38.360 --> 00:51:43.580
I've given Hayate enough money to break his debt to you.

00:51:44.330 --> 00:51:46.700
You understand what this means, don't you?

00:51:47.370 --> 00:51:51.330
Hayate has no need to continue as your butler.

00:51:52.080 --> 00:51:54.500
That's why he won't come to save you.

00:51:55.000 --> 00:51:57.260
T-That's not true!

00:51:57.260 --> 00:52:01.010
Hayate always comes to save me when I'm in trouble!

00:52:01.380 --> 00:52:03.600
Milady? You have a call from your butler.

00:52:03.600 --> 00:52:04.850
I got a signal!

00:52:04.430 --> 00:52:07.220
Milady? You have a call from your butler.

00:52:05.220 --> 00:52:07.850
I told you he'd call!

00:52:07.220 --> 00:52:10.310
Milady? You have a call from your butler.

00:52:08.600 --> 00:52:09.850
Is that right?

00:52:09.850 --> 00:52:11.730
I wonder if that means he's going to come here though.

00:52:10.310 --> 00:52:11.730
Milady?

00:52:12.310 --> 00:52:14.770
Hayate? It's me, Hayate!

00:52:14.770 --> 00:52:18.780
Hello, Milady! This is Klaus.

00:52:18.780 --> 00:52:21.110
Some gifts arrived for you from Amazon—

00:52:21.110 --> 00:52:21.610
Bah!

00:52:25.530 --> 00:52:28.410
I broke my iPhone!

00:52:28.410 --> 00:52:29.790
Hayate!

00:52:30.540 --> 00:52:31.750
Milady!

00:52:32.120 --> 00:52:34.630
I told you to let me cut the watermelon!

00:52:35.000 --> 00:52:38.130
It's all right! Just have a seat over there, Hayate.

00:52:38.550 --> 00:52:39.840
Gosh!

00:52:45.760 --> 00:52:47.310
<i>Huh? What am I...</i>

00:52:47.760 --> 00:52:50.060
<i>Wasn't there a...</i>

00:52:51.140 --> 00:52:52.520
<i>Umm...</i>

00:52:52.520 --> 00:52:53.900
Hayate?

00:52:54.270 --> 00:53:00.650
The others will be back soon, so can you help me set the table?

00:53:07.080 --> 00:53:09.040
Looks like he isn't coming after all.

00:53:09.410 --> 00:53:12.330
But there's still a chance.

00:53:12.330 --> 00:53:14.460
Hayate is a nice boy, after all.

00:53:16.290 --> 00:53:19.710
That's why I must make <i>sure</i> he forgets you.

00:53:21.920 --> 00:53:23.050
<i>Hayate!</i>

00:53:26.140 --> 00:53:27.180
Hayate?

00:53:29.720 --> 00:53:30.560
<i>Hayate!</i>

00:53:32.140 --> 00:53:35.980
Hayate!

00:53:38.610 --> 00:53:40.820
Hayate, Hayate!

00:53:42.570 --> 00:53:44.570
And you shouldn't throw things.

00:53:45.570 --> 00:53:47.320
All right, now give me your hands.

00:53:52.790 --> 00:53:55.330
You called, Milady?

00:53:55.710 --> 00:53:57.080
Milady!

00:54:02.920 --> 00:54:05.180
W-What's going on?

00:54:10.810 --> 00:54:12.350
W-What's that?!

00:54:12.680 --> 00:54:14.600
Everything's collapsing!

00:54:14.600 --> 00:54:16.020
It's dangerous! Get over here!

00:54:26.610 --> 00:54:27.700
I don't believe it!

00:54:27.700 --> 00:54:30.580
Reality is interfering with this world!

00:54:30.580 --> 00:54:34.830
I don't have the power to save you.

00:54:35.370 --> 00:54:39.580
What? So you really didn't want to kill me after all?

00:54:40.630 --> 00:54:41.840
You knew?

00:54:42.250 --> 00:54:45.840
If you did, you could have killed me long ago.

00:54:46.380 --> 00:54:51.390
Besides, this amusement park you made was a lot of fun.

00:54:51.390 --> 00:54:55.480
I don't think you could've made it so much fun if you really were evil.

00:54:57.980 --> 00:55:00.480
You're quite calm, aren't you?

00:55:00.480 --> 00:55:05.490
Do you still think Hayate will come here and save you?

00:55:05.490 --> 00:55:07.150
I do!

00:55:07.150 --> 00:55:10.870
Hayate always comes to save me when I'm in trouble!

00:55:25.550 --> 00:55:28.010
Why are they chasing us?!

00:55:28.510 --> 00:55:31.010
What in the world is going on?!

00:55:36.640 --> 00:55:38.020
We're surrounded!

00:55:40.020 --> 00:55:42.400
I can't take this anymore!

00:55:50.360 --> 00:55:53.410
I trust the two of you are unscathed.

00:55:53.910 --> 00:55:55.660
This way! Hurry!

00:55:56.620 --> 00:55:57.950
Isumi!

00:56:04.710 --> 00:56:06.050
There doesn't seem to be a blind spot.

00:56:06.050 --> 00:56:07.300
Yeah.

00:56:10.840 --> 00:56:12.470
What is it, Kayura?

00:56:19.810 --> 00:56:23.980
Can't you do something with that cosplay sword of yours?

00:56:23.980 --> 00:56:26.480
My Excalibur is made of cardboard!

00:56:28.650 --> 00:56:30.190
Miss Forehead!

00:56:54.470 --> 00:56:55.350
Are you all right?

00:56:57.810 --> 00:56:59.310
Hina!

00:56:59.310 --> 00:57:00.850
Miss Invincible!

00:57:02.980 --> 00:57:05.940
Hina! You came to save us!

00:57:06.980 --> 00:57:08.320
But where's Nagi?

00:57:09.400 --> 00:57:10.360
Nagi is...

00:57:10.780 --> 00:57:12.450
Nagi's in there!

00:57:19.330 --> 00:57:22.250
And how do you think he's going to save you now?

00:57:22.500 --> 00:57:24.370
Hayate will think of something!

00:57:24.750 --> 00:57:28.630
Hayate isn't bound by his debt any more.

00:57:29.340 --> 00:57:31.760
The debt that made him suffer for so long.

00:57:32.670 --> 00:57:34.680
The source of his hardships.

00:57:34.680 --> 00:57:37.390
The lock on his freedom and future.

00:57:38.100 --> 00:57:42.020
The cruel debt that my son put on his shoulders.

00:57:43.480 --> 00:57:47.520
With all of that gone, do you still think he will come?

00:57:47.520 --> 00:57:49.230
I will!

00:57:49.230 --> 00:57:50.690
For I am her butler!

00:58:05.580 --> 00:58:06.540
Hayate!

00:58:07.580 --> 00:58:09.790
I'm sorry to have kept you waiting, Milady.

00:58:09.790 --> 00:58:11.590
Hayate!

00:58:12.920 --> 00:58:14.970
Hayate, you...

00:58:15.930 --> 00:58:18.550
Excuse me, Milady.

00:58:26.890 --> 00:58:30.980
I know you gave it to me, but I must return it.

00:58:31.480 --> 00:58:32.070
But...

00:58:33.230 --> 00:58:40.580
I'm sorry to say this, Milady, but I decided I really want to pay off my debt by myself.

00:58:41.490 --> 00:58:43.700
Is that all right with you?

00:58:44.660 --> 00:58:46.710
Yeah! I'll be waiting!

00:58:49.130 --> 00:58:52.840
B-But that doesn't help your predicament!

00:58:52.840 --> 00:58:58.340
You'll be trapped by money again! Every day of your life will be unlucky again!

00:58:58.760 --> 00:59:02.720
I'll admit that life isn't easy...

00:59:04.470 --> 00:59:07.980
but I have someone who saved me from that.

00:59:32.920 --> 00:59:35.550
It's time to go, Milady.

01:00:14.790 --> 01:00:15.920
Where are we?

01:00:15.920 --> 01:00:19.420
Are these... the ruins of an amusement park?

01:00:22.590 --> 01:00:25.180
But why are they here?

01:00:26.720 --> 01:00:32.190
It was built during the economic bubble, but there were no visitors so it was closed.

01:00:33.440 --> 01:00:35.860
You know this place, Hayate?

01:00:36.230 --> 01:00:36.940
Yes.

01:00:36.940 --> 01:00:39.570
I've been here once before.

01:01:00.380 --> 01:01:03.880
That... was my last memory of this place.

01:01:04.430 --> 01:01:05.430
Hayate!

01:01:06.350 --> 01:01:07.850
Nagi!

01:01:08.810 --> 01:01:11.230
Hayate!

01:01:12.560 --> 01:01:15.900
Why are you all here so early in the morning?

01:01:15.900 --> 01:01:17.980
What were you doing?

01:01:18.480 --> 01:01:20.990
No, umm, how do I put it...

01:01:22.650 --> 01:01:25.240
Now that you mention it, what <i>were</i> we doing?

01:01:25.240 --> 01:01:27.330
It feels like I was dreaming.

01:01:27.330 --> 01:01:29.490
Yeah, it was a dream, wasn't it?

01:01:29.740 --> 01:01:32.290
But we went through all that effort to save you.

01:01:32.290 --> 01:01:34.540
You don't even remember?

01:01:35.080 --> 01:01:36.330
Effort?

01:01:36.330 --> 01:01:39.210
It became a wonderful memory.

01:01:40.760 --> 01:01:44.260
Anyway, everybody, breakfast is ready.

01:01:44.260 --> 01:01:46.010
Shall we go back and have some?

01:01:46.430 --> 01:01:47.970
Let's go!

01:01:47.970 --> 01:01:50.510
Now that she mentioned it, I'm rather hungry.

01:01:51.180 --> 01:01:52.730
Indeed!

01:01:52.730 --> 01:01:54.560
Umm, Hayate?

01:01:54.560 --> 01:01:58.060
I think I saw a really weird dream, myself.

01:01:59.070 --> 01:02:00.270
Weird, how?

01:02:00.650 --> 01:02:03.860
Umm... No, never mind!

01:02:03.860 --> 01:02:05.400
It's just a dream!

01:02:08.280 --> 01:02:11.370
Milady, shall we head back too?

01:02:12.580 --> 01:02:13.830
Milady?

01:02:14.830 --> 01:02:16.790
You know something, Hayate?

01:02:16.790 --> 01:02:18.040
Yes?

01:02:18.040 --> 01:02:24.550
I don't really... hate that woman or anything, you know?

01:02:25.090 --> 01:02:28.090
I mean... umm... I mean!

01:02:28.090 --> 01:02:31.470
That amusement park was sort of fun.

01:02:31.470 --> 01:02:32.310
So...

01:02:32.770 --> 01:02:35.560
Thank you, Milady.

01:02:37.310 --> 01:02:40.310
I think she was glad to hear you say that.

01:02:41.610 --> 01:02:42.320
Really?

01:02:42.780 --> 01:02:44.780
Then let's go back.

01:02:44.780 --> 01:02:46.450
Of course, Milady.

01:02:55.830 --> 01:02:56.910
Thank you.

01:02:57.460 --> 01:02:59.630
I'll be fine.

01:03:01.170 --> 01:03:03.090
Hey, Hayate!

01:03:03.090 --> 01:03:04.090
Coming!

01:06:13.610 --> 01:06:15.740
Jesus, that was awful.

01:06:15.990 --> 01:06:17.990
What are you going to do about my car?

01:06:18.320 --> 01:06:21.120
Don't worry, I'll have it pulled out later.

01:06:21.120 --> 01:06:22.330
Really?

01:06:22.330 --> 01:06:25.750
Are you really gonna get it pulled out from the bottom of that lake?

01:06:25.750 --> 01:06:28.500
I just pulled <i>you</i> out, didn't I?

01:06:28.500 --> 01:06:29.290
Same shit.

01:06:29.290 --> 01:06:30.750
How strong do you think you are?!

01:06:31.630 --> 01:06:33.260
Wait, isn't that impossible?

01:06:34.590 --> 01:06:37.220
Oh, shut up already! I'm sorry, okay?

01:06:37.800 --> 01:06:39.890
Here, take this in return.

01:06:39.890 --> 01:06:41.180
What are you doing?

01:06:45.430 --> 01:06:46.270
What's this?

01:06:46.690 --> 01:06:48.770
I found it in the water.

01:06:48.770 --> 01:06:50.400
There's a gem inside.

01:06:54.360 --> 01:06:55.530
There really is!

01:06:55.530 --> 01:06:56.950
There really is a gem!

01:06:57.740 --> 01:06:59.410
I wonder if this is worth anything.

01:06:59.410 --> 01:07:04.830
I dunno, but if it's a diamond, you can buy another car with the dough, can't ya?

01:07:04.830 --> 01:07:06.870
Go get it valued later.

01:07:10.670 --> 01:07:11.790
You idiot!

01:07:11.790 --> 01:07:14.210
I'm not gonna sell something you gave me!

01:07:15.970 --> 01:07:18.090
Anyway, let's find us some treasure!

01:07:18.090 --> 01:07:19.130
Treasure!

01:07:20.550 --> 01:07:21.300
Okay.

01:07:23.890 --> 01:07:25.720
Hurry up already!

01:07:25.720 --> 01:07:27.180
I'm coming!

01:07:27.180 --> 01:07:29.230
By the way, where the hell are we?

01:07:29.230 --> 01:07:30.230
How should I know?!

01:08:20.320 --> 01:08:23.160
I wonder whose feelings will come true this year.

01:08:23.530 --> 01:08:25.120
Just one person's feelings?

01:08:25.120 --> 01:08:26.740
It's like a lottery.

01:08:29.460 --> 01:08:30.620
Yes.

01:08:30.620 --> 01:08:31.710
Just one.

01:08:31.710 --> 01:08:34.080
And it has already come true.

01:08:45.850 --> 01:08:47.770
Your hands are sticky again.

01:08:49.310 --> 01:08:50.770
Oh, shut up!

01:08:57.980 --> 01:09:00.110
Here, give me your hands.

01:09:00.110 --> 01:09:01.030
I'll wipe them.

01:09:13.620 --> 01:09:14.540
Hayate?

01:09:15.880 --> 01:09:16.920
What is it?

01:09:19.250 --> 01:09:20.420
Thank you.

01:09:20.960 --> 01:09:23.300
You're welcome, Milady.
